. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H3 * (Please adapt according to your needs)
. 
.         * Please add a verbal description of your model here
. 
.         * As an example, and for illustrative purposes we consider a: linear 
> OLS regression
. 
.         * We estimate the causal effect of having a first daughter on the une
> qual division of housework within households using the Callaway and Sant’Anna
>  (2021) difference-in-differences estimator.
.         *The outcome variable housework_unequal captures the extent to which 
> housework is unequally divided between partners and treatmetn assignment stag
> gered across households over time.
.         *We use the doubly robust inverse probability weighting method (dripw
> ) to estimate group-time average treatment effects, comparing each treatment 
> cohort (defined by the timing of the first daughter) to an appropriate contro
> l group of not-yet-treated households.
.         csdid housework_unequal log_hghinc age age_man num_daughters num_sons
>  pgpsbil pgpsbil_man pgemplst pgemplst_man, ivar(hid) time(year) gvar(event_y
